    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43515" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔβοτ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βόσκω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>abounding in pasture</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.406
			</span></i> (or, <i>with fine oxen</i>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοτόν</span> (<span class="entity">Addenda</span>)); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς ζῴοις πᾶσιν εὔβοτον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Criti.</u>
					111a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.669
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cam.</u>
				16
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Scymn.
				607
			</span></i>, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1083.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>well-fed, thriving</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμνός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					5.24
				</span></i>
			.</div>
